OL,3,GNEWSANew apple named after road where
OL,4,Ait was discovered
OL,5,
OL,6,FA previously unidentified apple variety
OL,7,Fgrown in a back garden has officially
OL,8,Fbeen named after the road where it was
OL,9,Fdiscovered.
OL,11,FThe apple, now known as the Clarendon
OL,12,FBlush, was found on Clarendon Road in
OL,13,FLuton in 2023.
OL,15,FAccording to community project Luton
OL,16,FOrchards, 719 people voted in a public
OL,17,Fpoll to name the new apple and the name
OL,18,Fwas then approved by the Register of
OL,19,FLocal Cultivars.
OL,23,APub: 12-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB E Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
